+            // `frameStartedLoading` clears the frame's lifecycle set, and a
+            // same-document navigation (e.g. `Page.navigate` to `page.html#2`
+            // while on `page.html`) never re-fires `Page.lifecycleEvent`
+            // "load". `frameStoppedLoading` is the only signal that the frame
+            // is loaded again; without it the NavigationWatcher never sees
+            // "load" and `Page::goto` hangs until the request timeout, while
+            // every later navigation queues behind it.
+            // `FrameManager::on_frame_stopped_loading` already existed for
+            // exactly this (as in Puppeteer's `_onLoadingStopped`) but was
+            // never dispatched.
+            CdpEvent::PageFrameStoppedLoading(ev) => {
+                self.frame_manager.on_frame_stopped_loading(ev);
+            }
 
